---
// Refund and cancellation policy. Written for ADR 0014's license, when Paddle's
// domain review expected Terms, Privacy and a Refund Policy each reachable from
// the navigation; /terms still links here. Licensing is retired (ADR 0031), so
// the page now says what applies to a purchase made before that.
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Nav from "../components/Nav.tsx";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Refunds · Hostbeam"
  description="Hostbeam no longer sells anything. How a license bought before November 2026 is refunded."
>
  <div class="site" id="top">
    <Nav />
    <main class="wrap" style="max-width: 720px; padding-top: 64px; padding-bottom: 96px">
      <p class="note">Refund and cancellation policy · last updated 8 November 2026</p>
      <h1 class="h2" style="font-size: clamp(32px, 4.5vw, 48px)">
        Nothing is sold, so there is nothing to refund.
      </h1>
      <p class="lede" style="margin-top: 20px">
        Hostbeam is free: every feature, no limit, no reminder, on the Mac and the iPhone.
        Licenses are no longer sold.
      </p>

      <section style="margin-top: 40px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px">
        <h2 style="font-size: 20px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--ink); margin: 0">Bought a license before?</h2>
        <p style="margin: 0; color: var(--ink-soft)">
          Licenses were sold until November 2026 through
          <a href="https://paddle.com" style="color: var(--beam)">Paddle</a>, the merchant of
          record, under
          <a href="https://www.paddle.com/legal/checkout-buyer-terms" style="color: var(--beam)">Paddle’s buyer terms</a>.
          A key you activated keeps working, and the app has every feature either way, so a
          refund changes nothing in the app. If you want one for a recent purchase, email
          <a href="mailto:support@hostbeam.app" style="color: var(--beam)">support@hostbeam.app</a>
          with the email you bought with or the receipt, or go through
          <a href="https://paddle.net" style="color: var(--beam)">paddle.net</a> directly.
          Refunds go back to the original payment method; Paddle processes them.
        </p>
        <h2 style="font-size: 20px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--ink); margin: 12px 0 0">The iPhone app</h2>
        <p style="margin: 0; color: var(--ink-soft)">
          Free, with nothing to buy inside it, so there is nothing to refund there either.
        </p>
      </section>
    </main>
    <Footer />
  </div>
</Base>
